WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.323
[MUSIC].

00:00:06.323 --> 00:00:11.767
15,678 miles, 116 days,

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:18.101
35 states, one very dusty Honda Civic.

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:21.228
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:00:21.228 --> 00:00:26.400
&gt;&gt; This is the road trip that changed my
life.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.490
This road trip started with one goal.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.600
For me to land a job, as a local newspaper
reporter.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.990
But it lead me to much more.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.650
It lead me to a new way of living.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.710
This road trip way of living.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:49.250
Is about having the guts to take that
first step.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.800
It's about being open, and embracing the
unexpected.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:02.200
And it's about taking the time to slow
down and reflect.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.059
Get on the road.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.050
Embrace the detours.

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:10.740
Slow down once in a while.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.950
Let me tell you a little bit about life
before this road trip.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.339
I left a good job in network television to
go to journalism school in New York City.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:29.050
By 2003, I graduated with a dream of
becoming a newspaper reporter,

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:36.060
but newspaper jobs were scarce in New York
City, and

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.670
as hard as I tried, I had no idea how I
was gonna get hired.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.120
I felt paralyzed.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:50.180
Stuck in my shoebox sized studio apartment
in Greenwich Village,

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:51.900
glued to my tiny Ikea couch.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:57.930
I was going nowhere.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.590
How was I gonna get a job?

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:03.450
I had never been paid to write an article
before.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:08.630
Had no published clips, no big New York
City newspapers is gonna hire me.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:14.290
I spent days, let's be real,

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:19.500
weeks sitting on this couch in this New
York City apartment, the rising heat

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.516
of this New York City summer, and finally
I had, had enough of going nowhere.

00:02:24.516 --> 00:02:27.701
It clicked.

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:33.550
What if, instead of reaching out to the
big editors at the big papers,

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:36.210
I reached out to editors in smaller towns.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:36.970
Face to face.

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:43.520
At a small town, I could be, have my, my
own beat.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.900
My own byline.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.220
I could have my own voice.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.930
And so I prepared to hit the road.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:55.420
I took out a loan, I bought a car, boom.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:56.215
I was committed.

00:02:56.215 --> 00:02:56.813
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:02:56.813 --> 00:03:00.538
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I bought a giant laminated map of
the U.S.,

00:03:00.538 --> 00:03:05.470
I put little yellow dots of each town that
looked interesting.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.010
I would go South.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:12.390
And then West, I'll be on the road for 18
days, or so I thought.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.340
I'll never forget that feeling of
exhilaration as I drove

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:22.780
across the George Washington bridge, my
new Honda Civic packed to the windows!

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.250
I was exhausted, from days of preparation.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.070
But thrilled to finally be on the road.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.677
Finally I was moving forward.

00:03:33.677 --> 00:03:36.533
[BLANK_AUDIO].

00:03:36.533 --> 00:03:41.000
In life we're taught to strategize, to be
deliberate.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:46.350
Whether it's a job, a relationship, a new
home.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.100
We really like to know what to expect.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:58.860
But sometimes, the best decisions we can
make are based on no data at all.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.860
Sometimes, you need to just push paralysis
aside.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.304
And just get moving.

00:04:06.304 --> 00:04:11.135
Just go somewhere, anywhere.

00:04:11.135 --> 00:04:16.200
Sometimes you need to just get on the
road.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:19.170
So that's what I did.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.610
I followed that map, I went south,
Virginia, North Carolina,

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.030
South Carolina, Georgia.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.820
I had my moot routine, I was gaining
momentum.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.540
My process was locked.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:34.830
Reach out to those editors, plan those
informational interviews,

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:39.270
show up in town, check into the Motel Six,
show up for

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:42.470
the interview, and be ready for the
inevitable question.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.130
What are you doing here?

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:53.930
Why on earth would you leave New York City
and network television?

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:59.800
Do you really think this roadtrip is gonna
get you hired?

00:05:01.628 --> 00:05:06.170
I would [SOUND] work my charm as best I
could,

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:11.106
smile, shake hands, write thank you notes.

00:05:11.106 --> 00:05:14.040
I kept on moving.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.740
This was my plan.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.310
Dot after dot on the map.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:19.660
Finally I got to Tennessee.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:23.270
And the editor there suggested I reach out
to the sister paper in Little Rock.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.510
But Little Rock wasn't on my original map.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.360
I had already made plans to go to
Louisiana, Alabama,

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.800
I had to get up to Missouri, all within a
matter of days.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:38.250
Little Rock would be an inconvenient
squeeze.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:47.280
I'm not exactly sure why, but I ended up
adding Little Rock to my agenda.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.210
A few days later I rolled into town, it
was late at night,

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.130
I checked into the first hotel I could
find.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:59.090
The next day, I was pleasantly surprised
at the reception I got at

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.140
the Little Rock Newspaper.

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:04.380
The editor there was younger than most I
had met before.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.430
He had reddish hair, a broad smile.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.840
And when he showed me around this news
room, and

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:14.260
its lofty ceilings and sky lights, there
was an energy to the place.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.330
The buzz of reporters working on
deadlines.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.460
I sat down for an, an interview with that
editor.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.920
He didn't ask the usual questions.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:27.300
He didn't think this road trip was such a
crazy idea.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:30.700
In fact he was impressed with it.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.280
He was impressed with me.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:40.460
He told me there were no available
positions at the time.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.970
But he would reach out if anything opened
up.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:47.090
And finally I felt like somebody
appreciated my efforts.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:54.358
Finally I felt like I was making progress
and this detour, was paying off.

00:06:54.358 --> 00:06:57.933
[BLANK_AUDIO].

00:06:57.933 --> 00:07:03.603
Sometimes, the most amazing destinations
in life,

00:07:03.603 --> 00:07:06.756
are not on our original maps.

00:07:06.756 --> 00:07:09.277
[BLANK_AUDIO].

00:07:09.277 --> 00:07:12.490
When was the last time you ditched your
Google calendar, and

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.571
made time for something spontaneous?

00:07:14.571 --> 00:07:17.031
[BLANK_AUDIO].

00:07:17.031 --> 00:07:21.272
When was the last time you put down your
iPhone long enough to have a conversation

00:07:21.272 --> 00:07:22.233
with a stranger?

00:07:22.233 --> 00:07:25.157
[BLANK_AUDIO].

00:07:25.157 --> 00:07:26.540
These.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:31.040
A, opportunities for unexpected
interactions are everywhere.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.070
They happen all day.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:36.080
Dozens if not hundreds of opportunities to
make these connections.

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:42.930
It's up to us to be open to these
opportunities,

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:45.380
meaningful ones, when they arrive.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.286
That's how it is on this road trip way of
life.

00:07:49.286 --> 00:07:52.502
[BLANK_AUDIO].

00:07:52.502 --> 00:07:56.403
You get on the road, and you embrace the
detours.

00:07:56.403 --> 00:07:59.060
[BLANK_AUDIO].

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:02.240
So after Little Rock, I kept moving west.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.010
By then I was sporting.

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.705
Pretty serious left arm tan.

00:08:05.705 --> 00:08:06.280
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:12.680
&gt;&gt; And often, I was driving for miles with
nothing but static on the radio.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:18.410
I took this time to conduct my own sort of
interview.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.830
I took my time to ask myself.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:22.600
The tough questions.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:27.390
I realized this road trip was giving me
the freedom to figure out what I

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:28.160
really wanted.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:34.020
And I checked in to realize that I
actually did want to live in a small town,

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:35.990
because I wanted to have a big impact.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:41.700
I wanted to make sure that I worked with
colleagues who actually appreciated.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:42.460
My experience.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:48.670
This is what I truly wanted, and after
many more miles,

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:52.470
many more interviews, I had found a new
focus.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:09:01.310
In my final states, just the last few
miles, I got a call back.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:05.720
From that editor, the one in LIttle Rock
who had been so impressed with me and

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:06.260
my road trip.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:10.780
By then, there were no more questions in
my mind.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:17.115
Yes, I said as he offered me a job as the
new Little Rock Prime reporter.

00:09:17.115 --> 00:09:19.560
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:21.165
&gt;&gt; That sounds perfect.

00:09:21.165 --> 00:09:22.524
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:25.180
Let's face it.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:28.650
Even the most amazing road trips can be
tedious at times.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:34.020
The roads can start to look the same.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:38.245
The Motel 6's, I can assure you, are all
identical.

00:09:38.245 --> 00:09:41.490
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:44.080
&gt;&gt; But there's value in this monotony.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.460
Value in these long stretches.

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:49.350
Value in having nothing else to focus on
but what is right in front of you.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:56.140
Some people find these moments in long
hikes, or meditation practice.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:03.070
Some people find this time on a cross
country plane ride, without WiFi.

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:07.230
The gurus call it mindfulness.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:10.890
Taking the time for the present moment and
your priorities.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:15.670
And for me, the road is my mindful place.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:22.420
My chance to slow down and reflect on what
truly makes me happy.

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:27.310
When it comes time for your next big,

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:32.730
life decision, remember this road trip way
of life.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:37.570
Maybe you're feeling stuck, paralyzed you
dont know what to do next.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:42.109
What if you push the risk assessments
aside?

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.610
And just got out there.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.760
And just got moving.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:50.670
Maybe you're already rolling full speed
ahead towards your final destination.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.410
You know where you need to go, nothing
will stand in your way.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:58.540
But if this is the case, ask yourself am I
on auto pilot?

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.828
Am I missing a chance for meaningful
detour?

00:11:02.828 --> 00:11:06.379
[BLANK_AUDIO].

00:11:06.379 --> 00:11:11.812
And every once in a while pause just long
enough to make

00:11:11.812 --> 00:11:18.100
sure that where you're headed truly feels
right in your gut.

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:24.790
It's up to you to make this time for the
reflection.

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:27.310
For the mindfulness, for yourself.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:35.100
Get on the road, embrace the detours, slow
down

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:44.645
once in a while.

00:11:44.645 --> 00:11:45.704
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE].

